      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--mm-feature-transport=cuda_ipc` was rejected on ROCm even though the implementation only uses PyTorch's CUDA-compatible APIs (`torch.cuda`, `_share_cuda_`), which dispatch to HIP IPC in a ROCm build. That forced every image feature tensor through the CPU shared-memory transport. On MI325X, a paired frontend profile attributed **0.73 s** to `wrap_shm_features` / `_wrap_shm_or_inline` for 128 concurrent image requests; HIP IPC wrapping is **0.02 s** (−97.3%).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Accept `cuda_ipc` on CUDA **or** ROCm/HIP in `_handle_multimodal_feature_transport`. The single-node and multimodal-splitting guards are unchanged, and the public flag name stays `cuda_ipc`.\n- Unit tests: ROCm acceptance (env-isolated with `patch.dict` — acceptance writes the legacy IPC env var and must not leak into later tests) and an explicit rejection test for non-CUDA-like platforms.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMI325X, Torch 2.9.1 + ROCm 7.2, BF16 (`HSA_ENABLE_IPC_MODE_LEGACY=1`):\n\n- `test/registered/unit/server_args/test_server_args.py` passes; cross-process `test_cuda_ipc_transport.py` passes.\n- Standalone HIP IPC probe — allocate → pooled share → reconstruct in a spawned process — returns the exact tensor (`torch.testing.assert_close`) with exactly one cached pool handle.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nSingle-image serving workload (512×512, 268 input / 32 output tokens, 512 prompts, 1 warmup + 3 measured runs, one MI325X):\n\n| Concurrency | CPU SHM | HIP IPC | Gain |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 16 | 1,374 tok/s | 1,649 tok/s | +20.0% |\n| 32 | 1,686 tok/s | 2,154 tok/s | +27.8% |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39094939664](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39094939664)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39094939726](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39094939726)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39094939657](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39094939657)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
